  }
 ],
 "guides": [
  {
   "uri": "opentally://guide/accounting",
   "name": "OpenTally accounting and report guide",
   "description": "Report date scope, amount formats, journal sides, and voucher identities.",
   "mimeType": "text/markdown",
   "text": "# OpenTally accounting guide\n\nOpenTally stores one INR company per DuckDB file. Write amounts are decimal rupee strings. Report fields with a _paise suffix are exact integer strings. Signed balances use debit positive and credit negative. A null opening or closing indicates unconfirmed data.\n\nDay Book accepts inclusive dates, status and voucher kind. Report row windows use offset and limit. Headline report totals cover the full result. Find ledger and voucher identifiers before opening detail tools.\n\nThe application validates balanced ordered postings, closed periods, bank matches and voucher revisions. Use a stable request UUID for voucher creation and retry. Edit and cancellation retain the previous revision."
  },
  {
   "uri": "opentally://guide/import-reconciliation",
   "name": "OpenTally import and bank guide",
   "description": "Import preview controls and bank match rules.",
   "mimeType": "text/markdown",
   "text": "# OpenTally import and reconciliation guide\n\nPreview the original Tally XML or OpenTally JSON text before choosing whether to persist an import. Supply its source company and a confirmed opening date when available. Check voucher and posting counts, debit and credit totals, duplicate and revised entries, and import warnings.\n\nBank CSV columns are transaction_id, date, amount, reference and description. Use an immutable source transaction ID and a YYYY-MM-DD date. Deposits are positive and withdrawals negative.\n\nA reviewed match can span multiple statement lines and postings. Both signed totals must agree. Match IDs identify the reconciliation group. Undo records the operator and reason and returns the underlying rows to review."
  }
 ]
